<script lang="ts">
	import Demo from "./demo.svelte";
</script>

# Toggle

A button that can be on or off, such as for bold text in an editor. Renders a `button` with `aria-pressed`. Give icon-only toggles an `aria-label`.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Toggle } from "#lib/components/ui/toggle/index.js";
	import { BoldIcon } from "@lucide/svelte";
</script>

<Toggle aria-label="Toggle bold"><BoldIcon /></Toggle>
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/toggle.json
```

## Outline

Set `variant="outline"` to add a border. The default variant is transparent until hovered or pressed.

<Demo section="outline" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Toggle variant="outline" aria-label="Toggle bold"><BoldIcon /></Toggle>
<Toggle variant="outline" aria-label="Toggle italic"><ItalicIcon /></Toggle>
```

## With text

Place text after the icon for a labeled toggle. It no longer needs an `aria-label`.

<Demo section="text" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Toggle variant="outline"><ItalicIcon />Italic</Toggle>
```

## Controlled

Use `bind:pressed` to read and set the state from your own code, or `onPressedChange` to run code when it changes. Without either, set `defaultPressed` to start pressed. A passed `onclick` runs first; call `e.preventDefault()` in it to keep the current state.

<Demo section="controlled" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Toggle } from "#lib/components/ui/toggle/index.js";
	import { BookmarkIcon } from "@lucide/svelte";

	let isBookmarked = $state(false);
</script>

<Toggle variant="outline" bind:pressed={isBookmarked}>
	<BookmarkIcon />
	{isBookmarked ? "Bookmarked" : "Bookmark"}
</Toggle>
```

## Disabled

Set `disabled` to dim the toggle and block interaction.

<Demo section="disabled" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Toggle disabled aria-label="Toggle bold"><BoldIcon /></Toggle>
```

## Sizes

Set `size` to `xs`, `sm`, `md`, or `lg`. The default is `md`, the height matches the button of the same size, and the corner radius follows the size.

<Demo section="sizes" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Toggle size="sm" aria-label="Toggle bold"><BoldIcon /></Toggle>
<Toggle size="lg" aria-label="Toggle bold"><BoldIcon /></Toggle>
```

## Rounded

Set `rounded` to `xs` through `4xl` or `pill` to override the radius from the size.

<Demo section="rounded" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Toggle variant="outline" rounded="pill" aria-label="Toggle bold"><BoldIcon /></Toggle>
```

## API

The `Toggle` props extend the native `button` attributes. It sets `data-state` to `on` or `off` for custom styles.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface Props extends CompPropsWithChild<"button"> {
	/** Whether the toggle is pressed; supports `bind:pressed` */
	pressed?: boolean;
	/** Starting state when `pressed` is not set; defaults to `false` */
	defaultPressed?: boolean;
	/** Called with the new state when the toggle is pressed or released */
	onPressedChange?: (pressed: boolean) => void;
	/** `default` is transparent until pressed; `outline` adds a border */
	variant?: "default" | "outline";
	/** Height, padding, text, and icon size on the shared scale; defaults to `md` */
	size?: UiSize;
	/** Corner radius; follows `size` when omitted */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
}
```
